From: cv610-fpv
Subject: [PATCH] hi3516cv6xx imx335: 2-lane 2x2 binning, 1296x972 up to 66 fps

On top of 0001/0002. Mode 1 (2x2 binning, full field of view) was a 4-lane
37.125 MHz table; it now uses the stock-firmware 2-lane 24 MHz INCK/analog
block (SYS_MODE 0x01, LANEMODE 2) with the ev200 binning registers, and
leaves the 4-lane MIPI timing (0x3A18-0x3A28) at its power-on values.

Binning reads 4H per output row, so it saves link bandwidth but not readout
time. Measured on a Hi3516CV610-20S + IMX335 2-lane board: VMAX 3900
truncates frames, and HMAX below the sensor minimum 0x113 (250, 230, 206)
streams at rate with a broken image. VMAX 0x0FD2 at HMAX 0x113 caps the mode
at 66 fps; 60 fps verified clean on waybeam and majestic.

--- a/libraries/sensor/hi3516cv6xx/sony_imx335/imx335_cfg.h
+++ b/libraries/sensor/hi3516cv6xx/sony_imx335/imx335_cfg.h
@@ -221,26 +221,53 @@
     {0x30E8, 0x00},    {0x30E9, 0x00},
 };
 
+/*
+ * 1296x972 2x2 binning, 10-bit, 2-lane (LANEMODE 0x3A01=1), INCK 24 MHz,
+ * 1188 Mbit/s per lane (SYS_MODE 0x01). The INCK/analog block is the
+ * stock-firmware 2-lane table of mode 0; the binning registers (WINMODE 0x01,
+ * 0x3300, Y_OUT, AREA2/3, 0x3078-0x3117, 0x3199) are the ev200 driver's
+ * binning_60fps table, whose 4-lane MIPI timing (0x3A18-0x3A28) is left at
+ * the power-on values the 2-lane mode uses. Full field of view.
+ * Binning still reads two sensor rows (4H) per output row, so it saves link
+ * bandwidth but not readout time: measured on the bench, VMAX 3900 truncates
+ * frames (963 of 972 rows) and any HMAX below the sensor minimum 0x113
+ * (250, 230, 206) streams at rate but with a broken image. VMAX 0x0FD2 at
+ * HMAX 0x113 caps the mode at 66 fps.
+ */
 static cis_reg_cfg imx335_binning_60fps[] = {
